# Update documentation after website edits

When you finish editing the ARL Online website (frontend, API, scripts, env, or structure), update the documentation before considering the task complete.

`AGENTS.md` is the map: it lists every doc and what belongs in it (**Start here**). Detail lives in the topic docs under `docs/`.

## Required

1. Read `AGENTS.md` at the project root before making structural changes.
2. After changes that affect behavior, layout, APIs, scripts, env vars, or directory structure, update the doc that covers it: `docs/frontend.md` (components, `src/lib`, auth, styling), `docs/backend.md` (`server.js`, API table, env vars, Docker / Cloud Run), `docs/consultations.md` (Expertise consultations), or `AGENTS.md` itself (directory layout, which code runs where, npm scripts, common change patterns).
3. Add a row at the top of the **Change log** table in `docs/changelog.md` (newest first) for meaningful changes.
4. If you change Expertise / consultation behavior, update `docs/consultations.md` (and `.cursor/rules/expertise-consultations.mdc` if invariants change). Also update `docs/automated-emails.md`, `docs/automated-webhooks.md`, or `docs/automated-notifications.md` when those triggers change.
5. Open bugs and owner to-dos live only in `docs/claude-handoff.md`. Delete an item there once it is fixed or done.

## Skip doc updates only when

- Typo fixes, comment-only edits, or formatting with no behavioral change.
- Dependency bumps that do not change how the app runs or is developed.

## Do not

- Leave any doc describing removed files, endpoints, or workflows.
- Put long detail in `AGENTS.md`; it stays a short map.
- Add new README or markdown files unless the user asked for them; prefer updating the existing docs.
